/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/subscript.k-25-  // ==== Subscript: indexing obj[i] (list / tuple / str) =====================
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/subscript.k-26-  // contexts (not strict attrs): the Index slot's Slice alternative must never heat
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/subscript.k:27:  context Subscript(HOLE, _)
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/subscript.k:28:  context Subscript(_:Val, HOLE:Expr)
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/subscript.k-29-
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/subscript.k-30-  // heap-object deref (covers both the index and slice forms via the Index slot)
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/subscript.k:31:  rule <k> Subscript(ref(H:Int), IX:Index) => Subscript(V, IX) ... </k>
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/subscript.k-32-       <heap> ... H |-> V:Val ... </heap>
