/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-73-  // RHS evaluates first (Assign strictness), then the key. Dispatch on the scope
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-74-  // value: a bare dict updates in the scope (dicts stay values); a ref (a heap
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-75-  // list — or a heap dict later) writes the heap in place.
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-76-  syntax KItem ::= #dsetK(String, Val)
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k:77:  rule <k> Assign(Subscript(Name(X:String), K:Expr), VV:Val) => K ~> #dsetK(X, VV) ... </k>
